    "planned_issue_append": {
      "transaction_state": "PENDING_ATOMIC_R53",
      "issue_id": "I000030",
      "unit_id": "tohoku:construction:extension-by-zero-support-limit",
      "status": "resolved",
      "kind": "source_missing_derived_functor_hypotheses",
      "claim": "The p. 220 passage passes from the degree-zero supported-section colimit to the derived formula (5.7.6) under only the neighbourhood condition on Psi, and later identifies colim_U H^q(X,A_U) with H^q_Phi(X,A). The first derived identification additionally requires Gamma_X^G-acyclicity of extension by zero on injective G-sheaves, while the ordinary supported-cohomology identification requires Phi to be paracompactifying; the three subsequent group-cohomology criteria supply neither hypothesis.",
      "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-equivariant-support-filtered-extension-by-zero;cohomology-lemma-equivariant-support-filtered-second-spectral-sequence",
      "evidence": "Official Part II SHA-256 8D632A04EE0FA987B40B721BEE6E64BB3E641D6A1CE02335556213F1564C9A53, printed p. 220, formulae (5.7.5)--(5.7.7 bis), states the neighbourhood condition before passing from the section colimit to (5.7.6) and later invokes the ordinary supported-cohomology colimit. The exact D1010 formalization block, 15171 bytes, SHA-256 EDED8F6FD2B6A1EF0CC0DDA6823219763EF51ED80D34FE3E56D51A4C116C84A4, separates Gamma_X^G-acyclicity of I_U for injective G-sheaves from the paracompactifying hypothesis on Phi and proves that conditions (a)--(c) concern only group-cohomology/filtered-colimit interchange.",
      "control": "Preserve the printed wording diplomatically. In corrected exposition and formalization, state the extension-by-zero acyclicity requirement for (5.7.6), state the paracompactifying requirement for the ordinary supported-cohomology comparison, and identify (a)--(c) as alternative criteria only for commuting group cohomology with the filtered colimit. D001024 resolves the missing-hypotheses issue; D001025--D001027 resolve the downstream spectral-sequence and interchange gaps without weakening either gate.",
